# ---- SECRETS / PERSONAL: never commit these ----
# NOTE: no trailing comments on these lines. In .gitignore a '#' only starts a
# comment at the START of a line -- written after a pattern it becomes part of
# the pattern, so the rule silently matches nothing. That exact mistake is how
# resume_data.json ended up committed despite "being ignored".
.env
cookies.json
# your real profile (resume_data.example.json is the template that IS committed)
resume_data.json
*.pdf

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE
.vs/

# Local run artifacts
debug/
applied_jobs.json

# Design reference screenshots (not part of the app / deployment)
dashboard/designs/
